<section class="section-line" id="topics">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow center">Topics</div>
    <h2 class="section-title center">Five messages, one God.</h2>
    <div class="onesheet" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <div><h3>Seventy Times Seven</h3><p>Peter's question, Jesus' answer, and the end of counting. The talk behind the book. Works as a single message or a three-part series.</p></div>
      <div><h3>The Battle for the Mind</h3><p>Repent, take every thought captive, be transformed. Three commands that turn out to be one campaign, with the Greek opened up.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Forgiving what can't be fixed</h3><p>When the apology never comes, the person is gone, or the damage is permanent. Forgiveness as release, not pretending.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Starting over at any age</h3><p>Job gone at fifty-eight, marriage over, seminary library, a book. What God does with a man who thought he was finished.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Prayer that moves</h3><p>Mark 11:22&ndash;25. The five necessities Jesus named during Passion Week, and why forgiveness is one of them.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Custom</h3><p>Tell me your theme and your room. I'll build to it. Men's events are where I'm most at home.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

